# Tests and CI Rules

Read `docs/05-TESTING-RELEASE.md` and `docs/06-CURSOR-WORKFLOW.md`.

- Add tests with the implementation, not as an afterthought.
- Run focused tests first, then full applicable validation.
- Idempotency is a hard gate.
- Detect check-mode mutation where practical.
- Prefer synthetic fixtures for state classifiers.
- Do not fake system integration by over-mutating a GitHub-hosted runner.
- Real SSH/firewall/systemd/Docker integration belongs on the Ubuntu 24.04 VM release path.
- Pin third-party GitHub Actions to full commit SHAs.
- Dependency bots may open PRs; do not configure dependency auto-merge.
- Never weaken or skip a security test merely to make CI green.
- Stop before merge/tag/release unless explicitly authorized.
